BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Books\, Bonds\, and Bereavement: Helping Siblings Process Loss
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T000000
DTSTAMP:20261008T061648Z
UID:2bffbc35a31244ac@gid-seminars.wnprc.wisc.edu
CATEGORIES:Class/Seminar
DESCRIPTION:OverviewThis activity explores the experiences and often-overl
 ooked needs of siblings of children with serious illness or medical comple
 xity. Faculty will discuss the emotional\, social\, and developmental impa
 cts of caregiving\, illness\, and bereavement on siblings and share practi
 cal strategies for supporting them as part of comprehensive family-centere
 d care. The session will also introduce bibliotherapy as an evidence-infor
 med approach to help siblings process grief\, normalize emotions\, and dev
 elop healthy coping skills through guided storytelling and discussion.\n\n
 RegistrationRegistration for all practitioners - free\n\nTo register for t
 his activity\, please click HERE.\n\nCreditsAMA PRA Category 1 Credits™ 
 (1.00 hours)\, ACPE Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, ANCC Contact Hours (1.00 
 hours)\, APA Continuing Education credits (1.00 hours)\, ASWB Continuing E
 ducation (ACE) credits (1.00 hours)\, CDR Continuing Professional Educatio
 n Units (1.00 hours)\, Non-Physician Participation Credit (1.00 hours)\, O
 ccupational Therapy Contact Hours (1.00 hours)\, Physical Therapy Contact 
 Hours (1.00 hours)\n\nTarget AudienceSpecialties - Adolescent Medicine\, A
 llergy\, Immunology\, & Rheumatology\, Anesthesiology\, Cardiovascular Hea
 lth\, Critical Care & Pulmonology\, Emergency Medicine & Trauma\, Hematolo
 gy\, Internal Medicine\, Neonatology\, Nephrology\, Neurology\, Oncology\,
  Pediatrics\, Psychiatry & Behavioral Sciences\, SurgeryProfessions - Fell
 ow/Resident\, Non-Physician\, Nurse\, Occupational Therapist\, Pharmacist
 \, Physician\, Psychologist\, Registered Dietitian\, Registered Nurse (RN)
 \, Social Worker ObjectivesAt the conclusion of this activity\, learners s
 hould be able to:\n1. Describe the emotional\, social\, and developmental 
 impacts of serious illness and bereavement on siblings\, including common 
 challenges and unmet needs.\n2. Apply evidence-informed strategies to supp
 ort siblings across settings by incorporating them into care conversations
 \, validating their experiences\, and coordinating with family\, school\, 
 a\n\nEvent URL: https://events.stanford.edu/event/books-bonds-and-bereavem
 ent-helping-siblings-process-loss\n\nSource: stanford_virtual
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/books-bonds-and-bereavement-helping-
 siblings-process-loss
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Reminder: Books\, Bonds\, and Bereavement: Helping Siblings Pr
 ocess Loss
TRIGGER:-PT1H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
